The rule for recover_json_object says: 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.' For the input fence[ S A ] B, the fence holds S and A, so the last object inside the fence is A. For the rewritten fence[ S A ] B with one part removed, the fence holds only S, so the last object inside the fence is S. The rule therefore says the recovered object moves from A to S. The kernel recovery should move.